.TH SIBYL 1
.SH NAME
sibyl, Sibyl, Review, quibble \- a programmer's assistant for Acme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sibyl
[
.B -e
.I effort
] [
.B -m
.I model
] [
.I instruction ...
]
.PP
.B sibyl -i
[
.B -w
] [
.B -s
.I n
] [
.B -e
.I effort
] [
.B -m
.I model
]
.PP
.B Sibyl
.PP
.B Review
[
.B -n
|
.B -s
] [
.I n
]
.PP
.B quibble -s
.I n
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sibyl
is a coding agent that Acme drives through files: its sessions are those of
.BR /mnt/sibyl ,
served by
.IR sibylfs ,
and the model's one tool, rc, is run by
.I sibylrun
as
.B none
in the name space
.I sibylns
makes: the user's tree to read, the project to write, no
.B /srv
or network.
.B doc/sibyl.md
has the design.
.PP
.I Sibyl
with no
.B -i
is a filter.
The instruction, then the text on standard input, are a turn; the answer comes on standard
output, and the commands the model runs, each after
.BR % ,
its output indented, on standard error.
As
.B |sibyl
in Acme the answer replaces the selection; Undo is its review.
Its commands change the project itself.
.PP
.B Sibyl -i
is a conversation, as
.B win sibyl -i
runs it.
A turn is what is typed up to a
.B ^D
(win's end of file); the reply follows a line
.B -->
and ends at a line
.BR <-- .
Delete cancels a turn, and
.B ^D
alone ends the session.
The session is kept in
.BI $home/lib/sibyl/ n\f1,
after a header of
.B dir
and
.B date
lines and a blank line;
.B -s
goes on with session
.IR n ,
showing its transcript and sending it ahead of the first turn.
A one-line turn
.BI /effort " e" \f1,
.BI /model " m"
or
.BI /prompt " file"
goes to the session's
.BR ctl ;
each alone shows the setting.
.PP
The commands of
.B sibyl -i
change the session's own copy of the project:
.IR cowfs (4)
serves the project with each change kept in
.BI $home/lib/sibyl/ n .tree\f1,
posted as
.BI /srv/sibyl. n .tree
while the session runs, so the real files, and Acme's windows on them, are as they were.
The model is told so
.RB ( /lib/sibyl/review )
and keeps
.B .cow/notes
in its copy: a summary, then a
.IB file : line
entry for each change worth explaining.
.B Review
in the window's tag, and the end of a turn that changed the copy, open the review.
With
.BR -w ,
the session is in place: its commands change the project itself, as the filter's do, the
header says
.BR "tree inplace" ,
and there is no review; Undo, or
.IR git (1)'s
diff, is the review.
.PP
.I Sibyl
lists the saved sessions in the window
.BR /sibyl/ ,
one a line: number, date, directory and first turn.
Button 3 on a line opens its session in a window of its own,
.IB dir /-sibyl. n\f1.
In the tag,
.B New
.RB [ -w ]
.RI [ dir ]
starts a session,
.B Delete
removes the sessions of the lines dot touches, with their copies, and
.B Get
lists them again.
.SS Review
.I Review
shows session
.IR n 's
changes, in the window
.IB dir /+review\f1,
.I dir
being its directory, the project.
With no
.IR n ,
it is the session of the window
.B $winid
names,
.IB dir /-sibyl. n\f1.
The window starts with the summary of
.BR .cow/notes ,
as
.B #
lines.
Then each changed file is a paragraph:
.B create
.I file
for a file the copy made,
.B delete
.I file
for one it removed, and the hunks of
.B diff -n -c
of the real file against the copy, each under the notes on its lines, as
.B #
lines.
A hunk's header names the real file on the left and the copy on the right, in
.IB file : lines " - " copy : lines
form, so button 3 on either opens it there.
The real file's text is its window's if it has one, else the disk's.
Notes on no hunk are listed last, after
.BR "# Other notes:" .
.PP
The window is a document: delete the hunks, or a file's paragraph, you do not want, and write
under the notes.
While it is open,
.I Review
watches the copy, and makes again the paragraph of each file that changes as the agent works,
keeping in it the lines you wrote and the hunks you deleted that are still the same; the
others are left as you have them.
In the tag:
.TF Discard
.TP
.B Apply
puts the hunks left in the window into the files' windows, each file's as one change, opening
a window for a file with none, and leaving them dirty for
.BR Put .
A file whose text, its window's or the disk's, is not what the copy began from, by the hash
.IR cowfs (4)
noted, is refused, and +Errors says which; so is a hunk that no longer fits.
A
.B delete
left in the window removes the file from the disk.
Applied hunks then match the window, and leave the review; the dropped ones stay in the copy, for
the agent to see and be asked about, until
.BR Discard .
.TP
.B Discard
empties the copy: the agent sees the real tree again.
.TP
.B Get
makes the window again from the copy.
.TP
.B Quibble
turns questions on and off, as
.B Indent
does indenting, saying which in +Errors; it is off when the window opens.
While it is on, a
.B #
line you type, ended with a newline, is a question: the note above it, its hunk and your line
go to
.IR quibble ,
and its answer is put in under your line as
.B #
lines.
Questions wait their turn, one at a time.
.PD
.PP
The next turn begins with what
.B Apply
did: the hunks applied, dropped and refused, and the lines you wrote, each under the note it
follows.
.PP
.B -n
prints the review and exits;
.B -s
prints a stamp of the copy, which changes when it does.
.SS Quibble
.I Quibble
is a filter, as
.B |sibyl
is, bound to session
.IR n ,
which must be open as
.BR "sibyl -i" :
the text on standard input is sent to the session as a turn of its own, an aside on
.B data
that the session's other readers pass over, and the answer is printed.
The session's window and transcript show the question and its answer as any turn.
.SH FILES
.TF $home/lib/sibyl/n.tree/.cow/files
.TP
.BI $home/lib/sibyl/ n
session
.IR n 's
transcript
.TP
.BI $home/lib/sibyl/ n .tree
its copy's changes, the shadow of
.IR cowfs (4)
.TP
.BI $home/lib/sibyl/ n .tree/.cow/fed
what
.B Apply
and
.B Discard
did, for the next turn
.TP
.B /lib/sibyl/prompt
the model's instructions;
.B /lib/sibyl/filter
and
.B /lib/sibyl/review
are added for the filter and for a session with a copy
.TP
.B /lib/sibyl/patterns
what of the tree the commands may read
.TP
.B /lib/namespace.sibyl
what is mounted for them
.SH SOURCE
.B /rc/bin/sibyl
.br
.B /rc/bin/quibble
.br
.B /acme/bin/Sibyl
.br
plan9web's
.B src/cmd/sibylfs
and
.B src/cmd/cowfs/Review.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR acme (1),
.IR cowfs (4),
.IR searchfs (4)
.SH BUGS
.I Review
watches the copy once a second.
A paragraph the agent changes loses your edits to its hunks, though not your lines.
A file whose window is closed after
.B Apply
and before
.B Put
is refused by the next
.BR Apply ,
since its disk text is not the one it noted.
